"Then you know the woman over the west gate begins work before sunrise. And that Hesset sometimes sleeps in his wagon. Which will be standing beside the other wagons."
{n}Hesset lowers his spoon.{/n}
"I hadn't got to that part."
{n}Varine looks toward Konomi. She does not immediately supply an answer.{/n}

{n}Hesset has arrived early, which makes him impatient before anyone else has had an opportunity to be late. His wagon carries four empty barrels and a crate of loose wooden pegs. Varine has paid a porter named Bel to move them into the store and back.{/n}
